<!--
  The works of a music box: a pinned barrel turning above a tuned comb, in its case.

  自鳴琴 is a koto that sounds itself, and this is the part that does the sounding — the pins
  set into the barrel, and the comb whose teeth they pluck as it turns. A note or a disc would
  have named the category; this names the thing.

  Drawn by hand and traced, so the line keeps its wobble. That is deliberate: the house style
  holds a hard, pared edge for anything that is an interface, and lets anything that is a mark
  be irregular and warm. This is a mark.

  The comb was drawn with eight teeth and carries four. At launcher size eight fell below one
  pixel of white between them and the whole comb went grey, which is the failure this icon
  had to survive; four teeth at twice the width keep the alternation of black and white that
  makes a comb read as a comb. Nothing else about the drawing was changed.

  Sized and placed by the circle that encloses it rather than by its bounding box, because
  the launcher's mask is a circle and a box-shaped drawing is exactly the case where the two
  disagree: centred on its box and scaled to the width the other icons use, this one had its
  corners cut off. Its enclosing circle is 62 of these 108 units across and sits on the middle
  of the canvas, which leaves the same margin inside the mask that Audio Reading has.

  It replaces CalmMusic's icon, by mostafaalagamy, which came over with the fork.
-->
